## 🇬🇧 English

<h3>🚀 About</h3>

I'm **Higer** ([@Higer23](https://github.com/Higer23)), a 16-year-old independent developer from **Dörverden, Lower Saxony, Germany**, building open-source software and hardware prototypes. I focus on **web applications, IoT systems, and automated hardware integration** — turning code into things that physically work, not just run on a screen.

Based in a charming riverside town on the Weser (approx. 40km southeast of Bremen), I combine rural innovation with modern tech. Everything here is developed in the open, documented honestly, and released under permissive licensing so other developers can learn from it, use it, or build on it directly.

**Current Projects:**
- **[Spende](https://github.com/Higer23/Spende)** — Donation/fundraising platform built with JavaScript
- **27+ active repositories** exploring web, hardware, and software integration
- 💭 **Bio:** I may be slow to respond, but I'm always working on something exciting!

